# Retention classes, the archive tier of the long class, and the overview of user rules.
admin-retention-classes = Retention classes
admin-retention-classes-intro = Each store belongs to a class. A class sets a ceiling in days; with the class limit switched on, a store's own limit is held to it. Long must not be below medium, and medium not below short.
admin-retention-class-short = Short: operational data
admin-retention-class-medium = Medium: security and sign-in history
admin-retention-class-long = Long: audit records and records of requests
admin-retention-class-short-about = Sessions, tokens, rate limits, job history and metrics.
admin-retention-class-medium-about = Sign-in history, request protection history, security notices and usage counters.
admin-retention-class-long-about = Security audit, administrator actions, data requests, consent records and tombstones. Can be moved to the sealed archive.
admin-retention-class-days = Ceiling: { $days } days.
admin-retention-class-days-forever = Kept forever.
admin-retention-class-enforce-on = The class limit is on: each store's own limit is held to its class ceiling, and 0 counts as the ceiling.
admin-retention-class-enforce-off = The class limit is off: each store keeps the limit set for it. The ceilings are shown for comparison.
admin-retention-exceeds-class = its own limit is above the class ceiling
admin-retention-archivable = can be archived
admin-retention-warn-mediumBelowShort = The medium class is set below the short class. It is raised to match.
admin-retention-warn-longBelowMedium = The long class is set below the medium class. It is raised to match.
admin-retention-warn-longForever = The long class is kept forever. Rows are never removed from the archive.
